From c7f43e6b92240547a6789b7a0e350ad7c9a8a320 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 07:39:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add persisted gamification (points, streak, badges) and fix
 two session bugs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Points and daily practice streak are now derived server-side from
ReviewEvent/Session rows (src/lib/gamification.ts) instead of only living as
ephemeral client state that reset every reload. Added a 7-badge starter set
and GET /api/gamification; wired into both the parent dashboard (stats +
badge shelf) and the child page (lifetime totals + unlock celebration),
alongside the existing session-local points/streak.

Also fixes two bugs surfaced while testing the feature end-to-end:
- GET /api/session/today's cached ("already built today") response never
  returned question content, only item ids — reloading mid-day showed "no
  items available" even with items left to do. Now hydrates the remaining
  items on that path.
- POST /api/reviews matched "today's session" by child+date only, so on a
  day with both a Maths and English session an answer could mark the wrong
  subject's session complete. Now matches on which session actually planned
  that item.

Also includes demo/recallie-kid-demo.html, a standalone no-build HTML mockup
of the child practice flow used to preview the UX (points, streak, confetti,
mascot) with real Week 1 sample questions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
